// Regression test (HYG-001): CFG::reportFlowDiagnostics() used to write
// unreachable-code and dead-branch warnings straight to std::cerr, bypassing
// DiagnosticEngine entirely -- no [E0NN] code, no color, no caret, no hint,
// even though UnreachableBlockWarning/DeadBranchWarning (ErrorsFlow.h)
// already existed fully written and were simply never constructed.
// Confirmed live before this fix: this exact function printed a plain
// "Warning: Unreachable code in block 'while.end' of function 'main'" with
// none of that. Now routed through the real warning classes, rendered like
// every other diagnostic, and registered as E074 ([E074] in the header,
// `turf --explain E074` works). Compilation must still succeed -- a warning
// never blocks compilation.
fn main(): int {
    while true {
        return 0;
    }
    return 2;
}
